  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n-(x+2)(x-4)\\ge 0,\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=-(x+2)(x-4)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/2bcb7336f352b1730a9c5b52060a4d49e9209cac73ca2688717f68c1af73168b.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-2\\le x\\le 4.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
